Z||000010||fierobear||07-22-2001||05:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88formula:<BR><B>Fiero 56, that is an interesting article, thanks for that information. My engine doesn’t lope or idle up and down when it is cold it just idles at a relatively steady 1500 rpm. It does idle a little erratic and it does occasionally misfire until it goes into closed loop. <P>87 FieroGTx anytime you want to go to the track or something I would be more than up to the challenge. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have the opposite problem. Mine has hunting idle from 600-1100 rpm after the engine is good and warm, and out of gear. Otherwise, no major problems.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||88formula||07-22-2001||11:31 PM||||Went through my first tank of gas. I traveled 197.7 miles and it took 10.54 gallons of gas to fill it up. That’s 18.75 miles to the gallon. Not bad for a new engine and all stop and go driving. ||||reg||1
